<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson restructuring Infocom systems.</title>
<headline>Ericsson restructuring Infocom systems.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson will save between 650 million and 800 million crowns annually by restructuring of its business area Infocom Systems, daily Finanstidningen said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;In total it is...reasonable to estimate that Ericsson in a short while has decreased costs in the troubled business area Infocom Systems by 650-800 million crowns annually,&quot; the Swedish business daily said.</p>
<p>Ericsson disclosed only that it would be at least 20 percent cheaper to manufacture the printed boards it has decided to outsource from its Norrkoping, Sweden plant to U.S. based SCI Systems, Inc and Solectron Corp.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
